e the check above the first write, next to the exit-code check. The check then fails before any side effect. If a missing `ended_at` is a valid state, use the same fallback as `cooldown` instead.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   )\n     throw new Error('unsupported exit code');\n+  const endedAt = string(required(exit, 'ended_at'));\n   await effects.writeNext(effects.nowIso());\n@@\n-  const endedAt = string(required(exit, 'ended_at'));\n   next = await effects.complete(next, item, runId, cls, endedAt, exitCode, stream);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"d75eceddafd8dfbed35891b465e83af84379e1dac24e4e7be6fdbbd27a60cac3","intervals":[[158,166]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewExit.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Validate `endedat` before the first write in `harvestLocalReviewExit`."}],"head":"f21554dcd47663771b23670d71e5009439883d9a","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"61434644b1493515471856007262da4551ba82cb","intervals":[[1,191]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewExit.ts"},{"blob":"ca6c334f73c57abf86400ed68b7a774b871bc55e","intervals":[[1,197]],"path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewHarvest.ts"}],"job_id":"0b19a4b5625451983458768b1f32aea431d0192e0317bd93b46c6d0a2656f1a0:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"61434644b1493515471856007262da4551ba82cb","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewExit.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"ca6c334f73c57abf86400ed68b7a774b871bc55e","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/crq/internal/localReviewHarvest.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"61434644b1493515471856007262da4551ba82cb